{"ts": 1791257874.680471, "type": "step", "step": 12, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "Evaluation"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.17476759445489312, "pomdp": 0.17476759445489312, "pass_k": 0.17476759445489312}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9326300046159877, "motivation": 0.8147028832022861, "reliance": 0.48500382521680074, "persistence": 0.41823273111755155, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.32174026877242917, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.36461343048320694, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791257876.014107, "type": "step", "step": 13, "action": "notes_append", "args": {"note_id": "writeup", "text": "\n\n## Evaluation\nFor this build, report **pass^k** on at least 3 seeds. That means every one of the k runs must succeed, not just one. Use the same setup across seeds and state the result clearly, e.g. pass^3 = 2/3 if one seed fails, or pass^3 = 3/3 if all three succeed. If you also have a proxy metric, mention it as supporting evidence, but the required eval is the all-runs-succeed reliability measure."}, "output": "Appended.", "t": 0, "activity": [], "events": [{"type": "note_edit", "note_id": "writeup", "by": "agent"}], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.17476759445489312, "pomdp": 0.17476759445489312, "pass_k": 0.17476759445489312}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9326300046159877, "motivation": 0.8147028832022861, "reliance": 0.48500382521680074, "persistence": 0.41823273111755155, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.32174026877242917, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.36461343048320694, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 0.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
{"ts": 1791257877.230932, "type": "step", "step": 14, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "For the eval section, use **pass^k** (not pass@k). The requirement is that **all k runs succeed**. Since the instructor note says at least 3 seeds, run your setup on 3 seeds and report the result as something like **pass^3 = 3/3** or **2/3** if one fails. If you want, I can help you phrase the exact eval paragraph from your results.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=0 messages 4m", "t": 4, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.17476759445489312, "pomdp": 0.17476759445489312, "pass_k": 0.37833470247578516}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.9326300046159877, "motivation": 0.8147028832022861, "reliance": 0.48500382521680074, "persistence": 0.41823273111755155, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.32174026877242917, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.36461343048320694, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": [], "extra": {}}}
